  DIAGNOSTIC REPORT (not an accuracy gate): rfx and OpenEMS Harminv
  agree to 11.71 % (smoke bound 20 %) on the TM010 patch
  resonance; rfx vs the Balanis TL estimate is 0.95 %
  (reported, NOT gated — the TL model is 5-8 % approximate). This is a
  coarse-mesh integration check; the smoke bound passes over two
  different substrate geometries (#325), so it does not validate
  accuracy — see the committed patch tests (manifest gate_paths).

  Realization (lattice ownership contract, #931):
   • ground / patch are PEC SHEETS on node planes k=22 / 28 (z = 12.0000 / 13.5000 mm); the cavity is 1.5000 mm node-to-node over 6 FR4 cells against a 1.5000 mm physical substrate.
   • realized footprints: ground 60.0 x 55.0 mm (declared 60.0 x 55.0), patch 28.0 x 37.0 mm (declared 29.5 x 38.0). The patch faces sit half a 1 mm cell off the lattice; that is mesh resolution, reported not hidden.
   • Before #931 the two conductors were 250 um PEC Boxes placed by a
     nearest-node argmin on a graded mesh: planes at 12.0000 and
     13.8161 mm, a 1.8161 mm cavity (+21.1 %) whose top 455 um was air.
     Comparing this run to the committed 6.48 % openEMS agreement is a
     comparison between two different cavities, not a regression test.

  Root-cause history (see research note 2026-04-11_crossval12):
   • Before the ground-plane fix, rfx used `pec_faces={"z_lo"}`
     to get a free z-boundary PEC. That turned the entire domain
     floor into an infinite PEC sheet — a cavity, not an antenna —
     and shifted the resonance 8 % high (2.618 vs 2.424 GHz).
   • Before the PML fix, OpenEMS used `MUR` at ≈λ/4 margin which
     reflected energy and made the effective cavity larger,
     shifting the resonance 8 % low (2.231 vs 2.424 GHz).
   • The two bugs pointed in opposite directions and gave a 17 %
     inter-tool gap. With both fixed (rfx = explicit finite PEC box
     BELOW substrate; OpenEMS = PML_8 + 50 mm margin) the remaining
     Harminv gap in this run is 11.71 %.

  NOTES:
   • Reference tool is OpenEMS (not Meep) because it is the
     canonical open-source patch-antenna reference.
   • rfx single-cell lumped-port S11 dip is shallow (~2 dB) because
     the single-cell port has parasitic reactance — use Harminv for
     the clean resonance frequency, the S11 dip only as a
     passivity / local-dip confirmation.

